  "summary": "My array of experiences as an independent software developer would prove useful to any team looking to round out its skillset. The type of work I did at CJM Enterprises, in addition to developing Pawn 3000, included both technical writing of instructional and promotional materials and copy editing of an industry newsletter.\n\nEverywhere I have worked I’ve done a lot of typing, proofreading, and business writing on behalf of team members whose skills were more tightly focused in other areas. During my time in the Lay Science Lab I also learned to wash scientific glassware in sulfuric acid, and while the use case for this skill may be quite narrow it does demonstrate my commitment to doing any job necessary to make your company successful.\n\nI am confident I can do any task that requires fast memorization of technical information and its synthesis into simple, easy-to-understand language and procedures. I can also simultaneously type and proofread, a skill at least one member of any effective team should possess. I believe my balanced combination of coding, writing, and clerical skills can be a great asset. I could also write music if that's really necessary. Whatever your company needs, I'm ready to work.",
